WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.030
After Dr. Wakaoji asked her what
she wanted to convey with "Eternal Snow,"

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.800
Mitsuki found an old music box
inside the storage shed.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.030
It was a present that Mitsuki's father
gave to her mother a long time ago.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:14.430
Takuto's Death Spirit Powers
revive the music box

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:16.360
and the melody to
"Eternal Snow" comes out.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.800
After hearing this, Mitsuki discovers
her message.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.900
So, I wonder what's going to
happen today...

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.700
Got that?

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:29.730
Yes.

00:02:02.230 --> 00:02:03.930
In this week's guest corner,

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:07.000
we have in our studio
Full Moon and Madoka Wakamatsu,

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:11.160
who will be competing with
their renditions of "Eternal Snow."

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.600
How are you two doing?!

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.660
- Hello.
- Hello!

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.060
Wow, so cute!

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.260
What are you holding
on your chest, Madoka?

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:22.730
Yes, this is my friend,
Gu the piglet.

00:02:24.330 --> 00:02:27.260
How cute that
a piglet is your friend.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.460
Thank you very much!

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.400
By the way, are you two doing
the recording on the same day

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:35.960
at the same studio
in this competition?

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:36.830
Yes.

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.660
Since it is the same song,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.830
will they actually be
completely the same?

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.560
No, I believe that both the
arrangement and the image

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.100
will be very different.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.030
Then, specifically,
how will it turn out?

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:51.030
That is a secret.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:52.760
Oh, that's too bad.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.060
How is yours progressing,
Full Moon?

00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:57.900
Is it secret with you too?

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.660
Oh, that's not the case at all.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:05.160
Tell you the truth, there's nothing
to even keep a secret about.

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.800
Huh? Really?

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.600
Yes. Actually, I haven't
been told anything.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.830
Umm... Isn't your producer

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:15.200
a former member of Route L,
Mr. Oji?

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:19.560
Yes, Mr. Oji has only
told me to think very hard

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:23.000
about what I want to convey
in this song.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.230
And what do you want to convey?

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:29.730
More than anything else,
I've been thinking

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.330
that I want to warm people's
hearts with music.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.800
I see, to warm hearts.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.430
Maybe that is Mr. Oji's goal.

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:40.160
What? Do you think so?

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.400
Thank you very much
for your hard work!

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:50.930
Thank you very much!

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:58.630
Miss Sasaki, what was
with today's interview?

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:02.700
Wasn't my part short compared
to Full Moon's?!

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:06.860
Sorry, with the appearance of Oji,
the director suddenly...

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.430
The appearance of Oji?

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:14.460
<i>Does Oji draw that much</i>
<i>more attention than Mr. Takasu?</i>

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:16.560
Miss Wakamatsu!

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.700
Do you have some time?

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:21.060
Excuse me! Please stop it.

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.730
Didn't I tell you that we're not going
to take your magazine's coverage?

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.400
Umm... What's happening?

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:26.830
Everything's fine, Madoka.

00:04:26.860 --> 00:04:31.030
He's from a tabloid magazine that
writes about scandals of young talents

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:33.130
and he's our enemy, so to speak!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:36.660
That's rude, do you need
to say it to that extent?!

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.460
There are even stars that have
had their careers killed off

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:43.060
because of things written up in
this magazine, which were all lies!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.730
<i>Careers killed off?</i>

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:48.060
Miss Sasaki! Do you have some time?

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.130
Yes!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.630
Now, let's go!

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:51.800
Oh, yes.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:54.660
Huh?

00:04:59.130 --> 00:05:01.360
If you have any interesting
material related to stars,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.030
I welcome it anytime.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:05.960
I'll make sure to show my gratitude.
Okay, see you later!

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.760
Madoka? Hurry up
and come over here!

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:13.760
Oh, yes!

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.330
Mr. Oji, isn't it about time
to allow Full Moon to sing?

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:32.100
No, it's not that time yet.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:33.260
Why?

00:05:33.530 --> 00:05:35.060
Do you need a reason?

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:39.730
But Madoka Wakamatsu's side seems
to be rapidly progressing with their plan.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:41.200
It doesn't matter.

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:47.330
Mr. Oji, don't you think the
staff is feeling dissatisfied too?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:49.730
Full Moon surely feels that way too.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.300
Schedule time is being taken
up for the preparation,

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:54.700
but she hasn't been allowed
to sing at all.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:05:57.230
If she doesn't at least
do some warming up,

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.860
she won't suddenly be able to sing
in the actual take.

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:00.760
Do you think so?

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:01.430
What?

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.000
Don't worry. Please leave it to me.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.300
Oh...

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:10.700
Mr. Oji...

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.030
Don't you want to sing soon, Mitsuki?

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:19.800
Yes.

00:06:21.760 --> 00:06:24.760
<i>I wonder if the recording</i>
<i>is really going to be all right?</i>

00:06:26.260 --> 00:06:32.830
<i>I love you, my tears won't stop.</i>

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:36.960
<i>If this is how it's going to be,</i>

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.700
<i>I wish I had never met you</i>

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:43.230
It's no good, stop it.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:43.960
Yes sir.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.160
What's wrong, Madoka?

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.360
I'm sorry.

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.330
You're not being yourself.

00:06:55.160 --> 00:06:57.630
I fell in love with the
Madoka Wakamatsu

00:06:57.730 --> 00:07:00.660
who's filled with more
self-confidence and dignity.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.930
Yes, thank you very much.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.000
Get back your usual self
by the main take.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:07.600
Do you understand?

00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:18.400
Did you hear the story about
Full Moon's new song?

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:19.460
Huh? What, what?

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.530
After Mr. Oji signed
on as a producer,

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:25.630
many famous musicians
have asked to participate in it

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.260
and it's going to be
an awesome line-up!

00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.930
Wow, is that true?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.060
Then isn't Madoka Wakamatsu
in trouble?

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.800
It seems like Mr. Takasu is
going to completely lose face.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.330
Oops! Hush!

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:55.030
<i>What on earth am I doing wrong?</i>

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:58.930
<i>I don't understand what</i>
<i>Mr. Takasu is demanding from me.</i>

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:00.100
Huh?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.230
Didn't I tell you not
to nestle close to me

00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.160
when people are not looking?!

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:14.000
I'm only keeping you for
my image as a gentle, animal loving girl!

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.760
If you don't stop it,

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.800
I'll change your name
to "Yummy-looking."

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:21.060
Oh, darn it!

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:28.630
<i>I'm going to lose if it</i>
<i>stays like this.</i>

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:31.800
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:35.760
<i>Oh...</i>

00:08:36.600 --> 00:08:39.930
<i>If you have any interesting material,</i>
<i>I welcome it anytime.</i>

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:49.100
<i>There are even stars that</i>
<i>have had their careers killed off.</i>

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.560
Hello?

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.960
Is this Mr. Yomitani?

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:15.060
That doctor!

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.360
I wonder why he called you
out all of a sudden.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:21.460
I don't know. Maybe it's time
for him to finally let me sing.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:22.560
That's possible.

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:32.160
Mitsuki!

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:36.860
Dr. Wakaoji, I'm sorry I was late!

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:39.500
That's fine, but what did
you need to talk to me about?

00:09:40.530 --> 00:09:44.430
I came here because I was told
that you needed to talk to me.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:48.400
What? I came here because
I was called out by you.

00:09:48.760 --> 00:09:51.000
I was also told to come here.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:01.730
Who was that guy?

00:10:02.000 --> 00:10:04.000
What was that just now?

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:05.830
That's gonna be a problem.

00:10:06.060 --> 00:10:07.730
What? What do you
mean by "a problem"?

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:10.630
Anyhow, we should contact Ms. Oshige.

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:22.530
Who cares about the director?

00:10:22.930 --> 00:10:25.660
I have my own circumstances over here!

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:28.200
Old man, one more drink!

00:10:28.360 --> 00:10:29.200
Yes!

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:31.330
I'm not getting through to her.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:34.530
Dr. Wakaoji? What has happened?

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.400
Listen to what I say carefully.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:40.300
All right?

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:41.900
Yes...

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:05.400
Maybe I drank a bit
too much last night.

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:09.730
<i>It's this morning's</i>
<i>"Fresh-Picked Entertainment News."</i>

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:12.430
<i>We'll turn this corner over</i>
<i>to Mr. Kinoshita.</i>

00:11:13.160 --> 00:11:16.060
<i>Okay, now for</i>
<i>"Fresh Picked Entertainment News"</i>

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:17.360
- Huh?
- <i>and today's first story.</i>

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:19.730
- Mr. Wakaoji called me yesterday.
<i>- She's now the number one</i>

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:21.800
<i>pop idol, Full Moon.</i>

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:25.660
<i>The photo of her with the producer,</i>
<i>Mr. Oji, was published</i>

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.100
<i>in a weekly photo magazine</i>
<i>on sale today!</i>

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:28.830
What the—?!

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:31.700
<i>It happened at an Italian restaurant</i>

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:34.300
<i>famous for being</i>
<i>a date spot for celebrities.</i>

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.300
W-What...

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:38.600
What is this?!

00:11:41.730 --> 00:11:45.560
<i>Speaking of Full Moon's</i>
<i>companion producer Mr. Oji,</i>

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.660
<i>he used to play the</i>
<i>keyboard for Route L,</i>

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:51.430
<i>but has returned to the music industry</i>
<i>this time to produce for Full Moon.</i>

00:11:51.460 --> 00:11:52.900
BIG SCOOP!
FULL MOON (16) ON SECRET DATE
WITH HER PRODUCER

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:54.530
Wow, what is this?!

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:55.830
Isn't this it?

00:11:55.860 --> 00:11:57.700
The thing they were showing
on TV this morning.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.930
Yeah, yeah. Full Moon is
going out with the producer.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.860
What? That's so shocking!

00:12:03.230 --> 00:12:04.430
Hey, we're going.

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:05.430
Okay.

00:12:05.460 --> 00:12:06.660
And I liked her so much!

00:12:06.860 --> 00:12:09.960
What was that?
Did you actually have a photo taken?

00:12:10.100 --> 00:12:10.800
Yeah.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:13.000
Wait a minute! Isn't that bad?

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:13.900
Yeah.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:15.530
But...

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:20.400
<i>What happened just now</i>
<i>is like an accident</i>

00:12:20.430 --> 00:12:23.760
<i>that a young female singer</i>
<i>like you comes across now and then.</i>

00:12:24.530 --> 00:12:26.060
<i>Even if you're being careful,</i>

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:27.630
<i>an accident just happens</i>
<i>when it happens.</i>

00:12:27.730 --> 00:12:29.930
<i>You're not the one at fault.</i>
<i>Neither am I.</i>

00:12:30.130 --> 00:12:32.200
<i>We just had a little bad luck.</i>

00:12:32.530 --> 00:12:35.160
<i>People forget about</i>
<i>silly rumors quickly.</i>

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:39.400
<i>But you might need</i>
<i>some perseverance until then.</i>

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:43.400
<i>Mitsuki, do you think</i>
<i>you can handle it?</i>

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:46.130
<i>Yes.</i>

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:51.030
<i>Good, I'll be with you.</i>
<i>You don't need to worry.</i>

00:12:51.560 --> 00:12:52.300
<i>Yes!</i>

00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.200
So that's what happened.

00:12:56.560 --> 00:12:59.130
He's surprisingly dependable.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:05.500
Yes. I felt really glad that I asked
Dr. Wakaoji to produce for me.

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:07.200
I think so too.

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:09.530
<i>He is really an adult.</i>

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:11.430
<i>To tell the truth,</i>

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:14.200
<i>I didn't know what to</i>
<i>say at that time.</i>

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:19.030
What is this?
Isn't this a lack of oversight?

00:13:19.100 --> 00:13:20.160
I-I'm sorry.

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:23.400
First of all, I don't care
if it is Oji or whoever,

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:25.700
but is the recording actually
going to be done?

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:32.230
If I don't hear some material soon,
I won't know what to tell Mr. Miyata.

00:13:33.030 --> 00:13:34.500
Yes. That's...

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:38.230
SCOOP!
WE DELVE INTO
FULL MOON'S PRIVATE LIFE

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.660
<i>Will I be able to let go of</i>
<i>these thoughts of you?</i>

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:53.930
<i>Hold me tight,</i>
<i>if this is how it feels</i>

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:59.000
<i>to fall in love with someone,</i>

00:13:59.030 --> 00:14:01.630
<i>I wish I never knew.</i>

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:08.060
<i>I love you,</i>
<i>my tears won't stop.</i>

00:14:08.330 --> 00:14:10.230
<i>If this is how it's going to be</i>

00:14:10.260 --> 00:14:19.660
<i>I wish I had never met you.</i>

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.500
Umm... Mr. Takasu?

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:33.160
Huh? Oh yeah.

00:14:33.360 --> 00:14:35.260
<i>How was my singing?</i>

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:38.730
There's something that weighs
on my mind, no matter what.

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:39.530
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:41.530
Let's end it here for today.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:46.900
Mr. Takasu?

00:15:25.000 --> 00:15:27.060
I really want to sing this one song.

00:15:30.960 --> 00:15:34.260
<i>Grandma, please make sure</i>
<i>to listen to my song someday.</i>

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:36.660
<i>And please come to like,</i>
<i>even a little bit,</i>

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:38.860
<i>music that you've hated for so long.</i>

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.500
TODAY'S RECORDING SCHEDULE:
A. FULL MOON 1:00 - 6:00
B. MADOKA WAKAMATSU 1:00 - 8:00
There's a huge group of reporters.

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:53.260
That's because it's right after
Full Moon had that kind of a scandal.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:56.400
Mr. Oji seems to have
already entered.

00:15:57.130 --> 00:15:58.730
Will Full Moon come?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.560
Well, don't you think it's impossible?

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:03.200
There's even a rumor that
the release is going to be postponed.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.230
What?! Is that true?

00:16:06.000 --> 00:16:07.260
Good morning!

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:09.500
What? She's here?

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.400
Hello, I look for your guidance today.

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:17.230
Oh? Yes...me too.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:24.030
<i>Hey, how do you feel?</i>

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.560
I have so much desire
to sing right now,

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:29.230
I feel like my chest is
going to burst open!

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.830
Good, then let's begin.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:50.560
<i>The emotion that piled up inside me</i>
<i>while I didn't sing all that time...</i>

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:56.060
<i>I hope this song will warm</i>
<i>the hearts of people who listen to it.</i>

00:16:57.200 --> 00:17:00.360
<i>I hope they are wrapped up</i>
<i>by a warm happiness.</i>

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:09.830
<i>How long has it been</i>
<i>since I fell in love with you?</i>

00:17:10.660 --> 00:17:18.930
<i>My feelings keep getting stronger.</i>

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:28.030
<i>I wonder if you can notice them?</i>

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:30.500
<i>Even though</i>

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:33.260
- Can it be that...
- <i>I've never mentioned it,</i>

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:36.960
<i>I've never mentioned it,</i>

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:45.860
<i>they're silent like this snow.</i>

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:48.530
<i>But they...</i>

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:53.160
You planned it like this...
by not having her sing until now.

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:56.830
<i>...keep building up.</i>

00:17:57.300 --> 00:17:58.330
You really feel Full Moon's desire

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:01.500
- to sing the song.
<i>- Hold me tight,</i>

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:04.330
- I became quite nervous, but...
<i>- if loving someone</i>

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:12.730
<i>was going to feel like this,</i>

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:16.060
<i>I wish I never found out about love.</i>

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:23.000
<i>I love you, my tears won't stop.</i>

00:18:23.030 --> 00:18:24.530
Where is Mr. Takasu?

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:28.100
- He's late.
<i>- If this is how it's going to be,</i>

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.160
- Good morning, sir!
- Good morning, sir!

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:30.760
<i>I wish I never</i>

00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:31.960
- Mr. Takasu...
<i>- I wish I never</i>

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.200
- I look forward to your guidance today!
<i>- found out about love.</i>

00:18:34.200 --> 00:18:36.130
- Then let's begin at once.
<i>- found out about love.</i>

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:37.700
Madoka, be on stand-by.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:38.500
Yes...

00:18:40.300 --> 00:18:40.960
Madoka!

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:42.600
Yes!

00:18:43.160 --> 00:18:44.100
Please come over here.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:45.760
Yes.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.400
I thought about doing it
after the recording,

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:54.130
but I wanted to take it upon
myself to talk to you about it now.

00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:55.100
Yes.

00:18:57.430 --> 00:18:59.530
Do you not believe in me?

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:00.360
What?

00:19:02.630 --> 00:19:04.560
I heard about the story
from the editorial staff.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.730
Umm... There is a reason for this.

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:07.430
Reason?

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.000
Umm... Well, I mean...

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:12.100
What kind of reason is there?

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:19.260
In this world, no matter what
kind of dirty thing you do,

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:21.460
the one who's standing
in the end is the winner.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:24.660
I won't make a pretty statement like
saying that what you did is dirty.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.630
But you don't believe in me.

00:19:29.500 --> 00:19:30.330
That's...

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:33.260
I believed in you.

00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:34.100
Huh?

00:19:34.760 --> 00:19:36.230
I told you before.

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.030
I can only work with somebody
who believes in my skill.

00:19:40.200 --> 00:19:43.630
I intend to settle what happened
this time in my own way.

00:19:43.900 --> 00:19:45.160
What do you—?

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.500
We will perform the recording
as planned.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:53.430
But after today,
I will step down from producing you.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:12.960
<i>I believed in you.</i>

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:28.900
What in the world happened?

00:20:28.930 --> 00:20:30.060
I have no idea.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:31.330
Madoka...

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:34.200
Oh, Mr. Takasu...

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:37.860
What happened with
Madoka Wakamatsu?

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:39.800
I'm sorry, Ms. Oshige.

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:44.060
Mr. Takasu...

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:45.700
Madoka...

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:52.030
You should think hard one more time
about the reason why you want to sing.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:56.260
That's all I can say.

00:21:14.300 --> 00:21:19.100
<i>You should think hard one more time</i>
<i>about the reason why you want to sing.</i>

00:21:19.430 --> 00:21:21.300
The reason why I want to sing.

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:25.760
If I don't know that reason,

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:28.460
will I be unable to sing
like she was?

00:23:07.460 --> 00:23:11.360
The time's finally come for Meroko
to put on a stellar performance!

00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:13.400
Okay, okay.
So what's it this time?

00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:15.560
A school friend of Mitsuki
is confused

00:23:15.600 --> 00:23:17.800
and decided that she's
an expert in the matters of love

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:19.630
and is asking her for advice!

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:22.960
Huh? How could she
be an expert in love?

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:26.500
Right? And so it's now time
for me to help out!

00:23:26.860 --> 00:23:28.530
That is a bit weird too!

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:33.260
Next time on Full Moon:
"Is Mitsuki an Expert on Love?"

00:23:33.430 --> 00:23:34.530
- Look forward to it!
- Look forward to it!
